@startuml
title Validate and replace an activity
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EDF3F8
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #526477
skinparam ArrowColor #526477
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox

actor "User" as User
participant "ui:Ui" as UI
participant "ConsoleHelper" as Console <<class>>
participant "edit:EditCommand" as Edit
participant "activities:ActivityList" as Activities
participant "ActivityScheduleValidator" as Schedule <<class>>

Console -> UI : readLine()
User -> UI : edit 1 ...
UI --> Console : input
note over Console, Edit
  EditCommandParser validates input and creates the command.
  Parsing details are omitted here.
end note
Console -> Edit : execute(activities, storage)
Edit -> Activities : getByDisplayedIndex(...)
Activities --> Edit : original activity
alt original activity ends at or before now
  Edit --> Console : ended-activity warning
  Console -> UI : showMessage(warning)
  UI --> User : warning
else activity is eligible
  Edit -> Edit : combine fields and validate resulting times
  note right of Edit
    Invalid replacement values warn before mutation.
    The remaining path assumes valid values.
  end note
  Edit -> Schedule : validate(...)
  Schedule -> Activities : getCanonicalView()
  Activities --> Schedule : chronological activities
  Schedule --> Edit : valid or conflict warning
  note right of Schedule
    Always check duplicates.
    Require overlap approval only when the schedule changes.
  end note
  alt duplicate or unapproved time clash
    Edit --> Console : conflict warning
    Console -> UI : showMessage(warning)
    UI --> User : warning
  else validation succeeds
    Edit -> Activities : replaceByDisplayedIndex(...)
    Activities --> Edit : replaced
    Edit --> Console : result (didChangeActivities = true)
    ref over User, Console
      CompletionAndSaveSequence
      result, activities, storage
    end ref
  end
end
@enduml
